  "rationale": "The workflow already satisfies the dependency-caching optimization (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE) because `actions/setup-java@v4` is configured with `cache: 'maven'`, which caches the Maven local repository. The pattern's contraindication \"An equivalent cache already exists\" applies, so adding a separate `actions/cache` step for Maven would be redundant and would not preserve a meaningful gain. Other candidate patterns lack preconditions: there is no matrix for fail-fast, scheduled runs are historically successful (not repeatedly failing) so schedule suppression/pausing is not supported, and a custom timeout lacks sufficient cold-run duration history and risks interrupting valid slow builds that include CodeQL analysis and `mvn site`. No supported, safe change is identified.",
  "evidence_ids": ["pattern:P-LIT-GHA-CACHE"]
}
